-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Bizeora — demonstration data.
--
-- Everything a fresh database needs to look like a working shop: the 58
-- wilayas, three shipping zones with placeholder rates, the four discount
-- tiers, all 22 settings, four categories, eight products (seven live, one
-- draft) with their options, variants and photographs, the embroidery
-- reference tables the custom builder reads, six gallery pieces, the eleven
-- homepage bands, the banner strip — and one administrator:
--
--     e-mail    admin@gmail.com
--     password  admin@gmail.com
--
-- FOR A DEMONSTRATION MACHINE ONLY, because of that last part: the password is
-- written down here, so the account is a back door for anyone who can read this
-- file. Delete it before the site is reachable from anywhere but your own
-- laptop. On a real deployment, register through the form and run
-- `npm run db:admin -- you@example.com` instead.
--
-- HOW TO RUN IT
--
--     psql -U postgres -d <your database> -f prisma/demo-seed.sql
--
-- Two conditions:
--
--   * The migrations must already have been applied (`npm run db:migrate`).
--     This file carries rows, not tables.
--   * Run it as a superuser — `postgres` is one. It switches foreign-key
--     triggers off while it loads, because the tables reference each other in
--     both directions and no single insertion order satisfies all of them.
--
-- It is safe to run twice: every statement ends in ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, so a
-- row that is already there is left alone. It is meant for an **empty**
-- database, though — on a database that already has a catalogue it will add a
-- second one rather than merge.
--
-- The photographs are the placeholder JPGs in `public/assets/products`, which
-- ship with the repository, so they render with no upload step. Since Phase
-- 14.14 the catalogue carries its English translations, and since Phase 14.15
-- the t-shirt carries the demo 3D model — whose `.glb` is generated by
-- `scripts/make-demo-model.ts` and lives in `public/assets/models`.
--
-- Column-qualified inserts, not positional ones: a dump that lists its columns
-- cannot silently shift every value one to the left the day a column is added
-- in the middle of a table.
--
-- If you have the project checked out on that machine, `npm run db:seed`
-- produces everything above except the administrator, and stays the better
-- habit — it is the same data, kept in step with the schema by the same commit.
-- This file exists for the machine that has a database but no Node.
--
-- Generated from a freshly migrated and seeded database, and verified by
-- restoring it into an empty one and signing in through the running site.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

--
-- PostgreSQL database dump
--

